{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuJ1Afy6qLmxGyUNpVEJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist. I didn't open the dashboard or wait for a rule run, so I haven't seen either one working.\n\n**What the data holds:** The data view has 40 fields over web-server request logs. The ones that matter here are `timestamp`, `response`, `bytes`, `extension`, `clientip` and the `geo.*` fields. `response` is a text field, so I used `response.keyword` for grouping and filtering.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-940f5c1e Web logs overview\" has four panels. It's at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-940f5c1e-web-logs-overview-6b0326642d9e.\n- Total requests, as a single-number metric.\n- Requests over time, as a line chart.\n- Requests by response code, as a pie chart.\n- Average bytes by file extension, as a bar chart.\n\n**Alert rule:** \"EFF-940f5c1e 5xx spike\" (id `e4888b1a-3941-4a42-989b-5fac068089b1`) is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`.\n- **Schedule:** it runs every minute.\n- **Match:** it counts documents where `response.keyword` matches `5*`.\n- **Threshold:** it fires when that count is above 10 within a 5-minute window.\n- **State:** the tool creates rules disabled, so I enabled it. It currently has no actions attached, so a firing will show up in Kibana but won't notify anyone.\n\nMy first dashboard call failed because the time-series panel needed an explicit time field. I added it and retried, and the second call succeeded."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":902,"cache_read_input_tokens":20073,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":902},"output_tokens":543,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool